    "title": "Santa Rosa County holds amnesty day for hazardous waste - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gracie King ,\n1 hours ago\nSANTA ROSA COUNTY, Fla. ( WKRG ) — Santa Rosa County is set to hold a Household Hazardous Waste Amnesty Day on Saturday, Oct. 11, from 8 a.m. to noon.\nUPDATE: New video shows official punching suspect in head during immigration operation The event is free of charge and gives residents the opportunity to properly dispose of potentially hazardous materials at the Gulf Breeze Community Center, located at 800 Shoreline Drive, a Santa Rosa County release said.\nThe following items are accepted:\nUp to 10 regular car or truck tires per vehicle; no large, heavy-duty, or racing tires are accepted Up to five gallons of antifreeze, gasoline, paint, solvents, and oil (including cooking oil) Oil filters Lubricants Pesticides and fertilizers Pool chemicals and household cleaners Battery backups, rechargeable batteries (from vehicles, lawnmowers, laptops, cellphones, coin cells) No alkaline batteries ! Propane bottles Aerosol cans Flat-screen monitors and flat-screen TVs only Computers, laptops, tablets, cellphones Stereos, radios, amplifiers Printers, copiers, fax machines, circuit boards Power tools and extension cords DVD/DVR players Remotes and gaming systems Up to 20 fluorescent light bulbs Fire extinguishers Approved sharps containers – Bring a full, approved sharps container for proper disposal and receive a free replacement Car crashes into Crumbl cookie store in Mobile (photos) Small-quantity generators will also be accepted at a reduced rate.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
